WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:12.863
The API reference runs unauthenticated reads from the page: no signup, no credential, nothing that spends.

2
00:12.863 --> 00:21.863
What TAVONEL can read: the same list the upload route validates against.

3
00:21.863 --> 00:30.863
The deployment's own state, including that compiling your own files is not open here.

4
00:30.863 --> 00:38.075
A fixed product sample that shows the shape of an answer. Build against the shape; do not judge extraction from it.

5
00:38.075 --> 00:42.087
The response carries a Content-Digest header.

6
00:42.087 --> 00:50.089
Now a terminal. This screen replays a captured session: the commands that ran and the output they printed, unedited.

7
00:50.089 --> 00:58.092
The hash computed from the bytes received equals the Content-Digest the server stated.

8
00:58.092 --> 01:06.100
The published Python recipe is downloaded and matched against its hash in the channel manifest.

9
01:06.100 --> 01:15.110
The recipe recomputes the digest and prints each piece of evidence with the page and region it points at.

10
01:15.110 --> 01:21.112
The sample labels itself a product sample, not customer proof.

11
01:21.112 --> 01:27.623
The CLI file is matched against the channel manifest the same way.

12
01:27.623 --> 01:37.627
The CLI's status command runs without a key. It reports reading the public World as open, and compiling your own documents as closed.

13
01:37.627 --> 01:45.040
A finished Compiled World is open to read in full today. Compiling your own sources is set up with us.
